\pard{\f1\sect}\sectd\paperw12240\paperh15840\widowctrl\ftnbj\fet0\sectd\linex0\margl1440\margr1440\margt1440\margb1440\left\widctlpar\fi0\f2\fs18{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 2. Study Progress\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal9360\pichgoal11520 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
Days are from randomization time (negative are before). \line  \line \par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 3. Summary Study Progress (In-person Visits only)\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal4320\pichgoal7200 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
*NFP = No Further Progress: participants that haven't done the next visit, but have not dropped. \line Drop out rate percentages below are calculated without considering the “NFP” group. It is the percentage of those who dropped out of those who either dropped out or continued. \line  \line Drop Rate by Study Status: \line 	- After Randomization and before the next visit there was a 5% drop out rate. \line 		 - 5 dropped out of 110 participants who either dropped or continued. \line 	- After Week 8 and before the next visit there was a 7% drop out rate. \line 		 - 6 dropped out of 84 participants who either dropped or continued. \line  \line Based on the observed attrition rates, we would project that 106 of the subjects enrolled will complete the study (this includes the 78 who have already completed). \line  \line To reach the goal of 150 completed subjects, we estimate we need to enroll 50 more subjects, making 170 enrolled in total. \line  \line \par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 4. Subject Screening Numbers\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal7200\pichgoal7200 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
 \line  \line \par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 5. Enrollment Numbers\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal7200\pichgoal7200 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
First day is taken as 2024-01-01. Our target is to enroll 5 per month. \line  \line Our overall enrollment rate is 4.6 subjects per month and the rate for the last 3 months is 4.3 subjects per month. \line  \line \par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 6. Projected Enrollment\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal9360\pichgoal7560 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
*Current Status is the current number enrolled, 120, and the date data was pulled, 2026-03-10. \line **Targets is the targeted enrollment, 180, and the targeted end date, 2026-12-31. \line  \line At the current estimated pace of 4.74 enrollments per month we are projected to reach 180 by 2027-03-29, or projected to reach 166 by the end date, 2026-12-31. This estimated pace was produced with a weighted average of previous monthly enrollments and is recalculated on the 1st of each month. \line In order to reach the targeted 180 subjects (60 remaining) by 2026-12-31 we need to enroll 6.17 subjects per month. \line  \line Enrollment for the past 3 months \line 	Dec 2025: 4 \line 	Jan 2026: 5 \line 	Feb 2026: 6 \line  \line \par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20\b\s3 Figure 7. State of the Study\b0\line\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\pict\pngblip\picwgoal9360\pichgoal7560 }}\par}
{\pard\fi0\li0\f2\fs20
There are 109 subjects randomized that have not dropped. This figure includes the 78 subjects that have completed the study and the 31 subjects that are currently still in the study (i.e. have neither dropped nor completed). \line Based on the observed attrition rates, we would project that 28 of the 31 subjects that are on study will complete it, making a total of 106 completed subjects. \line  \line \par}
}
